DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
LOCATION:MAXWELL HALL
GEO:39.16705;-86.524718
SUMMARY:Healing Art Show 2026 Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Healing Art Show 2026  OPEN OCTOBER 2\, 2026 - OCTOBER 30 202
 6\, MONDAY - FRIDAY 12-4 PM  &#160\;The Healing Art Show Bloomington is a
  community art exhibit celebrating the connection between creativity\, me
 ntal health\, and well-being. Inspired by founder &amp\; coordinator Juli
 ette Kniola's experience seeing how art became a source of expression\, c
 onnection\, and joy for her sister while navigating mental health challen
 ges\, the show was created to bring greater awareness to mental health\, 
 normalize conversations about it\, and help reduce the stigma that too of
 ten surrounds it. First launched in October 2024 in alignment with World 
 Mental Health Day (October 10th)\, the Healing Art Show has grown into an
  annual community event supported by local artists\, organizations\, and 
 partners who believe in the power of art to bring people together.  Now i
 n its third year\, the Healing Art Show Bloomington invites artists to sh
 are work that reflects the many ways creativity can intersect with mental
  health and the human experience. Through a diverse collection of artwork
 \, the exhibit creates space for expression\, reflection\, connection\, a
 nd moments of joy— while helping people talk more openly about mental h
 ealth. Each year\, more artists and community members become part of the 
 show\, helping build a more open\, compassionate community where mental h
 ealth can be discussed without shame or stigma.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h3 class="title">  Healing Art Show 2026</h
 3><p class="subtitle">  OPEN OCTOBER 2\, 2026 - OCTOBER 30 2026\, MONDAY 
 - FRIDAY 12-4 PM</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p class="x_elementToProof"><span dat
 a-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">The Healing Art Show Bloomington is a com
 munity art exhibit celebrating the connection between creativity\, mental
  health\, and well-being. Inspired by founder &amp\; coordinator Juliette
  Kniola's experience seeing how art became a source of expression\, conne
 ction\, and joy for her sister while navigating mental health challenges\
 , the show was created to bring greater awareness to mental health\, norm
 alize conversations about it\, and help reduce the stigma that too often 
 surrounds it. First launched in October 2024 in alignment with World Ment
 al Health Day (October 10th)\, the Healing Art Show has grown into an ann
 ual community event supported by local artists\, organizations\, and part
 ners who believe in the power of art to bring people together.</span></p>
 <p class="x_elementToProof">  Now in its third year\, the Healing Art Sho
 w Bloomington invites artists to share work that reflects the many ways c
 reativity can intersect with mental health and the human experience. Thro
 ugh a diverse collection of artwork\, the exhibit creates space for expre
 ssion\, reflection\, connection\, and moments of joy— while helping peo
 ple talk more openly about mental health. Each year\, more artists and co
 mmunity members become part of the show\, helping build a more open\, com
 passionate community where mental health can be discussed without shame o
 r stigma.</p>
