DESCRIPTION:Today's 60-minute Virtual Information Session centers around 
 the Design-Build Studio\, an integral part of the Miller program curricul
 um. Faculty member Lucas Brown offers the presentation. The session will 
 also provide information on how to prepare your application. Bring your q
 uestions to the conversation.  The J. Irwin Miller Master of Architecture
  program is a three-year in-residence program\, with a two-year advanced 
 placement track possible for students who hold a B.Arch from a NAAB-accre
 dited institution or regional equivalent. With our twin studios approach\
 , students take visual art course alongside architectural studios to deve
 lop their style of architectural design. The three-year program welcome a
 pplicants from a variety of educational and career backgrounds.
