 n.</p><p class="p1">  After graduating with first-class honors in Fashion
  and Textiles from Gloucestershire College of Art and Design\, Bamber spe
 nt his early career honing his technical skills in Christian Dior's tailo
 ring and dressmaking workrooms and developing his now renowned eye for de
 tail. Subsequently\, Bamber worked as a costume designer for production t
 eams both in the U.K. and internationally and as senior designer with Cal
 vin Klein.</p><p class="p1">  Within five years\, Bamber joined Gucci to 
 rebuild the then-struggling brand. Working under Tom Ford\, Bamber was a 
 major contributor to the success of the brand and was seconded to both St
 ella McCartney and Yves Saint Laurent. During his tenure at Gucci\, sales
  increased from 230 million dollars in 1994 to almost 3 billion dollars i
 n 2003\, making Gucci one of the most profitable brands in the world.</p>
 <p class="p1">  Since leaving Gucci in 2006\, Bamber has consulted across
