 wn masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome
 . Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one ad
 ult for every 6 children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Through hands-on experiments with viewf
 inders\, pinhole cameras\, and cyanotype photograms\, students will disco
 ver how photography can document history\, reflect change\, and draw insp
 iration from nature. From framing a scene to harnessing the power of sunl
 ight\, we'll investigate how images are made and what they can communicat
 e. Join us to experiment\, observe\, and create your own light-powered ph
 otographs!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art educator for stud
 ents in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  M
 eet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum
  at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before exploring the g
 alleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll hea
 d back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpiec
 es! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. <str
 ong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, 
 with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
